Strength

Strong modular React architecture with clear separation (modules, services, hooks, barrel exports).

Modern, correct tech stack and proper project setup (Vite, React Router, Axios, ESLint).

Good routing foundation, service-layer pattern, custom hooks approach, and solid documentation.

Scalable structure suitable for team development.


Mistakes / Issues

Majority of core modules are missing or placeholders (Products, Cart, Orders, Drugs, Profile, Payments).

Shared components and utilities largely missing (Button, Loader, Navbar, validators, formatPrice, etc.).

Core infrastructure incomplete (http.js, appConfig.js, incomplete routes).

Services and hooks mostly stubs with no real logic, state, or error handling.

Naming inconsistencies and typos (Inventory folder case, ChatWithPharmicist).

Overall implementation is ~25–30% despite full structural planning.


Final Remark
Aaish, Abdullah, Yasir, and Osama demonstrate strong understanding of modular React architecture and professional project structuring. However, execution is significantly behind planning. The project is not production-ready due to missing modules, incomplete services/hooks, and absent core infrastructure. This reflects poor management and incomplete delivery rather than weak technical capability. With proper implementation effort, they can turn this into a strong project; in its current form, it remains an incomplete skeleton.